 the trailhead map, follow the signed loop with sturdy shoes, and stay off the fragile rock formations while hiking together.","short_summary":"A rocky woodland circuit around the park’s named sandstone formations.","evidence_claim":"The National Park Service identifies the Ledges Trail as a year-round 1.8-mile loop with no activity fee and no reservation requirement.","source_url":"https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/hike-the-ledges-trail.htm","source_title":"Hike the Ledges Trail","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2025-03-10","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"No activity fee or reservation; Cuyahoga Valley National Park charges no entrance fee. Use daylight hours because the parking lot closes at dusk.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"brandywine-gorge-loop-hike","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Brandywine Gorge Loop","title":"Loop Past Brandywine Falls","subtitle":"A waterfall-and-footbridge hike in the national park","notes":"Arrive early or late to improve parking odds, use the trailhead map, and keep the group on marked paths through the gorge.","short_summary":"A 1.5-mile gorge circuit with a waterfall overlook and creek crossing.","evidence_claim":"The National Park Service lists the Brandywine Gorge Loop as a year-round hike with no activity fee and no reservation requirement.","source_url":"https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/hike-the-brandywine-gorge-loop.htm","source_title":"Hike the Brandywine Gorge Loop","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2025-07-25","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"No activity fee or reservation; park entrance is free. The area closes at dusk, parking is limited, and the unpaved loop is not wheelchair accessible.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"beaver-marsh-towpath-walk","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Beaver Marsh","title":"Wildlife-Watch at Beaver Marsh","subtitle":"A short Towpath Trail walk from Ira Trailhead","notes":"Walk a quarter mile north from Ira Trailhead to the boardwalk, pause at the viewing platforms, and bring binoculars if you have them.","short_summary":"An easy out-and-back to wetland viewing platforms along the Towpath Trail.","evidence_claim":"The National Park Service recommends the Ira Trailhead-to-Beaver Marsh walk, lists the activity fee as none, and notes picnic, restroom, bench, and tactile-exhibit access.","source_url":"https://home.nps.gov/thingstodo/short-towpath-trail-walks.htm","source_title":"Short Towpath Trail Walks","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"No activity fee; Cuyahoga Valley National Park has no entrance fee. Leashed pets are allowed on the Towpath Trail but not in park buildings.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"boston-mill-visitor-center-exhibits","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Boston Mill Visitor Center","title":"Explore the Park Story Exhibits","subtitle":"Self-guided displays inside a restored 1905 store","notes":"Begin downstairs with the park overview, continue through the upstairs story exhibits, and collect free trail maps before heading out.","short_summary":"A self-paced indoor introduction to Cuyahoga Valley’s landscapes and history.","evidence_claim":"The National Park Service says visitors may explore Boston Mill Visitor Center’s exhibits at their own pace, with no activity fee, reservation, or park entrance charge.","source_url":"https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/stop-by-boston-mill-visitor-center.htm","source_title":"Stop by Boston Mill Visitor Center","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Free entry and no reservation. Visit during current visitor-center hours; store merchandise and food are optional purchases and unnecessary for the activity.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"canal-exploration-center-exhibits","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Canal Exploration Center","title":"Work Through the Canal Exhibits","subtitle":"Hands-on Ohio & Erie Canal history","notes":"Allow at least 30 minutes for the exhibits, compare favorite canal details, and use the trailhead kiosk for an optional Towpath walk.","short_summary":"An accessible, hands-on history session inside a former canal-side tavern.","evidence_claim":"The National Park Service describes the Canal Exploration Center as a hands-on exhibit visit lasting 30–120 minutes with no activity fee or reservation.","source_url":"https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/visit-canal-exploration-center.htm","source_title":"Visit Canal Exploration Center","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"No activity fee or reservation; the national park has no entrance fee. Check seasonal operating hours before leaving. The building is wheelchair accessible.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"east-rim-trail-mountain-bike","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"East Rim Trail System","title":"Ride the East Rim Loops","subtitle":"Intermediate single-track riding near Boston Mills Road","notes":"Bring your own bike and helmet, check the posted daily trail status, then follow the day’s one-way direction through an appropriate loop.","short_summary":"A fee-free group ride across four named, intermediate trail segments.","evidence_claim":"The National Park Service lists East Rim mountain biking as having no activity fee or reservation and identifies four trails for intermediate riders.","source_url":"https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/go-mountain-biking-in-cuyahoga-valley.htm","source_title":"Go Mountain Biking in Cuyahoga Valley","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2026-04-22","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"No fee or reservation when using your own bike; park entry is free. Trails may close in wet or icy conditions, so check current status first.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"howe-meadow-farmers-market-browse","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Cuyahoga Valley Farmers Market at Howe Meadow","title":"Browse the Howe Meadow Market","subtitle":"A purchase-optional seasonal market outing","notes":"Walk the vendor rows together, compare seasonal displays, and enjoy the market atmosphere without treating a purchase as part of the plan.","short_summary":"A free-entry browse through a seasonal national-park farmers market.","evidence_claim":"The National Park Service explicitly states there is no fee to attend Cuyahoga Valley Farmers Markets and that money is needed only if a visitor chooses to purchase something.","source_url":"https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/visit-cuyahoga-valley-farms-markets.htm","source_title":"Visit Cuyahoga Valley Farms and Markets","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2025-01-16","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Attendance requires no fee or reservation, and purchases are optional. Confirm the current market calendar and location before traveling.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
